    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The bug is fixed. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## Problem\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't passing the `--ci` flag to frai-gate, so the GitHub Actions workflow file wasn't being created, even though running `frai-gate init --ci` directly worked fine.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe frai CLI uses commander's `[args...]` pattern to capture arguments for the gate subcommand, but this only captures positional arguments\u2014not options like `--ci`. Commander parses options separately, and they weren't being passed through to the delegated frai-gate CLI.\n\n## Solution\nModified the gate command handler in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to pass all remaining command-line arguments from `process.argv` (which includes options) instead of just the positional arguments:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst passThrough = gateIndex >= 0 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : (args ?? []);\nconst result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...passThrough], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n```\n\n## Verification\n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- \u2705 `frai gate init` without `--ci` still works correctly (only creates `FRAI-SPEC.md`)\n- \u2705 Package rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`",
